%%label III. Andante con tenerezza
%%note F major, 5/4 (3+2). A song that opens with the motto's two rising fourths, first in the second violin, then in the first violin with a viola counter-melody; a restless middle section on the motto turned upside down; the song's opening returns in the minor at the climax and resolves into the major; the cello sings the whole song a last time.
X:1
T:Bernstein’s Missing Quartet
T:III. Andante con tenerezza
C:Lor, in the manner of Leonard Bernstein
M:5/4
L:1/8
Q:"Andante con tenerezza" 1/4=52
